<!--
  Trimming: the trim-analysis warnings found INSIDE EF Core's own three assemblies are not shown (module scope: these assemblies only; the
  warning ids are the ones EF Core 10 produces). Why it is safe: the three assemblies are not trimmed (IsTrimmable=false in
  TMPublisher.Desktop.csproj), so nothing they reach by reflection inside themselves is removed; the entity types are kept by the annotations
  of DbSet<T> and ModelBuilder.Entity<T>; our own model code is analysed like every other assembly. The assemblies outside EF Core it reflects
  into (System.Linq.Queryable, System.Linq, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite, Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Abstractions) are kept whole as well
  (TrimmerRootAssembly). The published program is run on the 0.1.5 test database by tools/check-published.ps1. A warning from any other
  assembly, or a new kind of warning from EF Core, still stops the build; if the SDK stopped reading _ExtraTrimmerArgs, these suppressions
  would fall away and the build would stop with the warnings (warnings are errors), not pass silently.
-->
